# Single-Developer Exception — <%= projectName %>

> **Regulatory reference:** §11.10(k) — Appropriate use of authority checks to ensure
> that only authorized individuals can use the system, electronically sign a record, access
> the operation or computer system input or output device, alter a record, or perform the
> operation at issue.

## Declaration

This document attests that **<%= projectName %>** operates under a single-developer exception
for regulated software development at governance level **<%= governanceLevel %>**.

Under this exception:

- The project's **arbiter review pipeline** serves as the declared rigor-equivalent reviewer
  (replacing human peer-review for routine changes)
- The developer's identity is bound to all git commits and signed artifacts via cosign keyless
  attestation using GitHub OIDC
- **All automated gates must pass** before any change reaches the main branch

